<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="sec" style="background:#FFFFFF">
<div class="in">
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px 72px;align-items:flex-start">
<div class="stack" style="flex:1 1 300px;min-width:0;gap:20px;max-width:380px" data-reveal>
<h2 class="h2" data-split>Aviation scheduling, answered</h2>
<p class="txt">Not sure Workofo fits your station? We'll show it with your own flight plan and rules.</p>
</div>
<div class="retail-faq" data-av-faq style="flex:2 1 520px;min-width:0" data-reveal>
<details><summary>What is aviation scheduling software?</summary><p>Aviation scheduling software builds rosters for ground staff around the flight schedule instead of fixed shift patterns. Workofo plans ramp, check-in, security and baggage teams in 15-minute intervals around every flight wave.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who is Workofo built for in aviation?</summary><p>Airport operators and ground handling providers that schedule large shift-based teams across terminals, stations and roles.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo handle delays and schedule changes?</summary><p>When the flight plan changes, Workofo re-plans the affected shifts and suggests changes, so supervisors don't rebuild the roster by hand.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Workofo plan around licences and certifications?</summary><p>Yes. Skills and qualification rules are part of every roster, so only staff with the right training are planned for each role.</p></details>
<details><summary>How much time can we save?</summary><p>Clients save up to 80% of the time spent on scheduling and admin. Labor savings depend on your operation, so book a call and we'll calculate them with your own data.</p></details>
<div class="retail-faq__more" data-av-faq-more hidden>
<details><summary>Does Workofo cover more than the ramp?</summary><p>Yes. Check-in, security, baggage handling and airport retail can be planned in the same system.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo follow working-time rules and union agreements?</summary><p>Yes. Rest periods, maximum hours and local agreements are applied to every roster.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do supervisors keep the final say?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo proposes the roster; supervisors review, adjust and publish it.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there an app for ground staff?</summary><p>Yes. Staff check rosters, share availability and trade shifts in the Workofo mobile app.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo connect to HR and payroll?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo connects to your HR and payroll systems, so approved hours flow straight to payroll.</p></details>
</div>
